{"name":"Cotton","hex":"#eeebe1","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Cotton","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["The name of several settlements around the world:\nA village and civil parish in Staffordshire Moorlands district, Staffordshire, England . \nA village and civil parish in Mid Suffolk district, Suffolk, England . \nAn unincorporated community in Mitchell County, Georgia, United States.\nA township and unincorporated community therein, in Saint Louis County, Minnesota, United States.","A village and civil parish in Staffordshire Moorlands district, Staffordshire, England ."]},{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A surname from Hebrew."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Cotton"}],"entries":[{"title":"Cotton","blocks":[{"text":"Cotton is a soft, fluffy staple fiber that grows in a boll, or protective case, around the seeds of the cotton plants of the genus Gossypium in the mallow family Malvaceae. The fiber is almost pure cellulose and may contain minor percentages of waxes, fats, pectins, and water. Under natural conditions, cotton bolls facilitate the dispersal of the seeds."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/68/CottonPlant.JPG/330px-CottonPlant.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cotton"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4e/BALLS_OF_COTTON_%28ANDHRA_-SOUTH_INDIA%29_READY_FOR_HARVEST.jpg/500px-BALLS_OF_COTTON_%28ANDHRA_-SOUTH_INDIA%29_READY_FOR_HARVEST.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4e/BALLS_OF_COTTON_%28ANDHRA_-SOUTH_INDIA%29_READY_FOR_HARVEST.jpg/1280px-BALLS_OF_COTTON_%28ANDHRA_-SOUTH_INDIA%29_READY_FOR_HARVEST.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4e/BALLS